    <summary>Alabaster 0.2beta - (from GridPlayer 0.5.5): play many videos side by side</summary>
    <description>GridPlayer Alabaster is a modified version of GridPlayer by vzhd1701: a VLC-based
media player that plays many videos at the same time in a configurable grid.

Version: Alabaster 0.2beta - (from GridPlayer 0.5.5). This is a pre-release.

VLC (libVLC) is bundled. The app has its own settings folder, installer id,
install folder (`C:\Program Files\GridPlayer Alabaster\`), Start menu folder
and file-type registrations, so it installs and uninstalls next to upstream
GridPlayer without replacing or removing it.

## Dependencies

- ffmpeg (ships ffprobe too): for streams whose sound comes as a separate file (planned merge feature)
- yt-dlp (the program): used when External yt-dlp is set in Settings; the app has a built-in yt-dlp module otherwise
- Deno: YouTube's JavaScript challenge, needed for YouTube streaming

Uninstalling alabaster-gridplayer leaves these shared packages installed.

## Notes

- Windows x64 only
- Installs via Inno Setup to `C:\Program Files\GridPlayer Alabaster\`
- Not the upstream `gridplayer` package
</description>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency id="ffmpeg" version="[9.0.2,)" />
      <dependency id="yt-dlp" version="[2026.10.26,)" />
      <dependency id="deno" version="[2.9.8,)" />
    </dependencies>
  </metadata>
  <files>
    <file src="tools\**" target="tools" />
  </files>
</package>
